FERROR(3)                      P32W Unix                       FERROR(3)

NAME
       ferror, feof, clearerr, fileno - stream status inquiries

SYNOPSIS
       #include <stdio.h>

       int ferror(FILE *f);
       int feof(FILE *f);
       void clearerr(FILE *f);
       int fileno(FILE *f);

DESCRIPTION
       ferror returns 1 if an error has occurred on the stream f (a
       failed read(2) or write(2), or reading a stream open only for
       writing, or the other way round), else 0.

       feof returns 1 if a read on f has met the end of the input,
       else 0.

       Both flags stay set until clearerr clears them; rewind(3)
       clears them too, fseek(3) and ungetc(3) clear the end-of-file
       flag.

       fileno returns the file descriptor under the stream, for use
       with the system calls (fstat(2), isatty(3), ...).

EXAMPLES
       while ((c = getc(f)) != EOF)
           ...
       if (ferror(f))
           fprintf(stderr, "read error\n");

SEE ALSO
       stdio(3), getc(3), fopen(3)

BUGS
       These are functions, not macros. The flags record that
       something failed, not what: errno, from the failed system
       call, may say.
